is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the bonded uplink interface (bond0) on sshswitch, which is the L2/L3 gateway for Campus 2 VLANs (10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24).

Mechanism: Campus 2 hosts can reach their gateways (br_v5 10.5.0.254, br_v6 10.6.0.254) locally on sshswitch, but anything off-subnet must traverse the uplink bridge br_v1 (55.5.1.0/24) to router17 (55.5.1.1). On sshswitch, bond0 is enslaved to br_v1 but is DOWN and its bridge port state is disabled, so ARP to 55.5.1.1 remains INCOMPLETE and traffic cannot exit Campus 2. Evidence: ip -br link on sshswitch shows “bond0 … state DOWN master br_v1”; ip -d link shows “bridge_slave state disabled” on bond0; ip neigh on sshswitch shows 55.5.1.1 INCOMPLETE and pings to 55.5.1.
