is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: sshswitch
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: the bonded uplink interface (bond0) on sshswitch, which is the L2/L3 gateway for Campus 2 VLANs (10.5.0.0/24 and 10.6.0.0/24).

Mechanism: Campus 2 hosts can reach their gateways (br_v5 10.5.0.254, br_v6 10.6.0.254) locally on sshswitch, but anything off-subnet must traverse the uplink bridge br_v1 (55.5.1.0/24) to router17 (55.5.1.1). On sshswitch, bond0 is enslaved to br_v1 but is DOWN and its bridge port state is disabled, so ARP to 55.5.1.1 remains INCOMPLETE and traffic cannot exit Campus 2. Evidence: ip -br link on sshswitch shows “bond0 … state DOWN master br_v1”; ip -d link shows “bridge_slave state disabled” on bond0; ip neigh on sshswitch shows 55.5.1.1 INCOMPLETE and pings to 55.5.1.1 fail. On router17, the peer (55.5.1.2) is also unreachable (ip neigh “FAILED”, ping to 55.5.1.2 fails), even though its bond0 is UP with eth0/eth1 slaves up. Physical members on sshswitch (eth6/eth7) show carrier up via ethtool, confirming this is not a cable/carrier failure.

Localization: sshswitch bond0 (slaves eth6, eth7) toward router17 bond0 (eth0, eth1).

Root cause: bond0 on sshswitch is administratively/operationally down while its slaves are up, leaving the bridge port disabled and cutting the uplink.

Corrective fix: on sshswitch, bring the master up (ip link set dev bond0 up) to re-enable the bridge port on br_v1; optionally configure bond monitoring (e.g., miimon 100) to prevent silent down states. Verify ARP completes (55.5.1.1) and end-to-end reachability returns.
=== END ===